<title>EGYPT: Yield rises on Egyptian 91-day T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Egyptian 91-day T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills rose to 8.940 percent from 8.923 percent at the previous auction on June 4..</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt had asked for 1.3 billion pounds and accepted bids for 1,458.775 million. Bills worth 872.950 million pounds mature on Thursday..</p>
<p>The Central Bank announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):.</p>
<p>Maturity date: Sept 11, 1997 (Sept 4, 1997).</p>
<p>Average yield: 8.940 percent (8.923).</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 1,458.775 million (1,441.375 million).</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1,535,825 million (1,755.500 million).</p>
<p>Range accepted: 8.499 - 9.006 percent (8.399 - 9.010).</p>
<p>Range of bids: 8.499 - 10.099 percent (8.399 - 10.002).</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 110 (87).</p>
<p>Number of bids: 115 (106).</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds.</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1/.</p>
</text>
